php artisan prisoner:add '{"name": "John Hill", "first_name": "John", "last_name": "Hill", "description": "Native American '\''Attica Brother'\'' (Dacajeweiah) who, The Black Panther Vol. 14 no.26 (1976) reports, was the only person imprisoned for an Attica-rebellion '\''crime'\'' — convicted of murdering a guard during the 1971 uprising and serving 20 years-to-life — even as the prosecutor recommended dropping all other inmate indictments. [Source: The Black Panther (Black Panther Party newspaper), v14 no.26; digitized at marxists.org — https://www.marxists.org/history/usa/pubs/black-panther/index.htm]", "aka": "Dacajeweiah", "state": "NY"}'

# Johnnie Harris (AL)
php artisan prisoner:add '{"name": "Johnnie Harris", "first_name": "Johnnie", "last_name": "Harris", "description": "One of the Atmore-Holman prisoners tried after the January 1974 Alabama prison rebellion; The Black Panther Vol. 14 (1975) reports he was convicted by an all-white jury of killing a guard and sentenced to death, and that his lawyers appealed on grounds of jury discrimination and the cruelty of the death penalty. [Source: The Black Panther (Black Panther Party newspaper), v14 no.4,9; digitized at marxists.org — https://www.marxists.org/history/usa/pubs/black-panther/index.htm]", "aka": "Johnny Imani Harris", "state": "AL", "affiliation": ["Inmates For Action"]}'

